usage: __main__.py [-h] [--video] [--video_length VIDEO_LENGTH]
                   [--video_interval VIDEO_INTERVAL] [--num_envs NUM_ENVS]
                   [--task TASK] [--frontend {torch,warp}] [--agent AGENT]
                   [--seed SEED] [--distributed]
                   [--run_timestamp RUN_TIMESTAMP]
                   [--max_iterations MAX_ITERATIONS] [--export_io_descriptors]
                   [--ray-proc-id RAY_PROC_ID]
                   [--capture_env_sensors CAPTURE_ENV_SENSORS]
                   [--capture_env_sensors_length CAPTURE_ENV_SENSORS_LENGTH]
                   [--capture_env_sensors_interval CAPTURE_ENV_SENSORS_INTERVAL]
                   [--capture_env_sensors_format {tensorboard,file}]
                   [--external_callback EXTERNAL_CALLBACK]
                   [--resume_optimizer_state | --no-resume_optimizer_state]
                   [--experiment_name EXPERIMENT_NAME] [--run_name RUN_NAME]
                   [--checkpoint CHECKPOINT]
                   [--logger {tensorboard,wandb,neptune}]
                   [--log_project_name LOG_PROJECT_NAME]
                   [--livestream {0,1,2}] [--xr] [--device DEVICE]
                   [--visualizer VISUALIZER] [--verbose] [--info]
                   [--experience EXPERIENCE] [--deterministic]
                   [--kit_args KIT_ARGS] [--anim_recording_enabled]
                   [--anim_recording_start_time ANIM_RECORDING_START_TIME]
                   [--anim_recording_stop_time ANIM_RECORDING_STOP_TIME]
                   [--max_visible_envs MAX_VISIBLE_ENVS]

Train an RL agent with RSL-RL.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --video               Record videos during training.
  --video_length VIDEO_LENGTH
                        Length of each recorded video clip in env steps.
                        Overrides the value in VideoRecorderCfg.
  --video_interval VIDEO_INTERVAL
                        Interval between video clips in env steps. Overrides
                        the value in VideoRecorderCfg.
  --num_envs NUM_ENVS   Number of environments to simulate.
  --task TASK           Name of the task.
  --frontend {torch,warp}
                        Runtime that constructs the environment. 'torch' uses
                        the registered stable environment via gym.make. 'warp'
                        (experimental) adapts a manager-based task config onto
                        the Warp runtime, or dispatches a direct task to its
                        registered Warp environment; requires
                        isaaclab_experimental and `physics=newton_mjwarp`.
  --agent AGENT         Name of the RL agent configuration entry point.
  --seed SEED           Seed used for the environment.
  --distributed         Run training with multiple GPUs or nodes.
  --run_timestamp RUN_TIMESTAMP
                        Timestamp naming the run folder; train_multigpu passes
                        one so that every rank shares the folder.
  --max_iterations MAX_ITERATIONS
                        RL Policy training iterations.
  --export_io_descriptors
                        Deprecated: export IO descriptors (removed in Isaac
                        Lab 3.2).
  --ray-proc-id RAY_PROC_ID, -rid RAY_PROC_ID
                        Automatically configured by Ray integration, otherwise
                        None.
  --capture_env_sensors CAPTURE_ENV_SENSORS
                        Number of environment views to capture from each
                        image-like scene sensor.
  --capture_env_sensors_length CAPTURE_ENV_SENSORS_LENGTH
                        Length of each captured sensor frame window (in
                        steps).
  --capture_env_sensors_interval CAPTURE_ENV_SENSORS_INTERVAL
                        Interval between captured sensor frame windows (in
                        steps).
  --capture_env_sensors_format {tensorboard,file}
                        Format used to save the captured sensor frames.
  --external_callback EXTERNAL_CALLBACK
                        Fully qualified path to an externally defined
                        callback.
  --resume_optimizer_state, --no-resume_optimizer_state
                        Restore the policy optimizer; disable to keep a fresh
                        optimizer and configured learning rate.

rsl_rl:
  Arguments for RSL-RL agent.

  --experiment_name EXPERIMENT_NAME
                        Name of the experiment folder where logs will be
                        stored.
  --run_name RUN_NAME   Run name suffix to the log directory.
  --checkpoint CHECKPOINT
                        Checkpoint path, latest/best, pretrained for play, or
                        a Weights & Biases run
                        (https://wandb.ai/<entity>/<project>/runs/<run_id>,
                        optionally with a '?checkpoint=<iteration>' query, or
                        the wandb:<entity>/<project>/<run_id> shorthand).
  --logger {tensorboard,wandb,neptune}
                        Logger module to use.
  --log_project_name LOG_PROJECT_NAME
                        Name of the logging project when using wandb or
                        neptune.

launcher arguments:
  Arguments for the KitLauncher. For more details, please check the
  documentation.

  --livestream {0,1,2}  Force enable livestreaming. Mapping corresponds to
                        that for the `LIVESTREAM` environment variable.
  --xr                  Enable XR mode for VR/AR applications.
  --device DEVICE       The device to run the simulation on. Can be "cpu",
                        "cuda", "cuda:N", where N is the device ID
  --visualizer VISUALIZER, --viz VISUALIZER
                        Visualizer backends to enable as CSV (e.g.,
                        kit,newton,rerun,viser).
  --verbose             Enable verbose-level log output from the
                        SimulationApp.
  --info                Enable info-level log output from the SimulationApp.
  --experience EXPERIENCE
                        The experience file to load when launching the
                        SimulationApp. If an empty string is provided, the
                        experience file is determined from the resolved
                        visualizer and XR settings. If a relative path is
                        provided, it is resolved relative to the `apps` folder
                        in Isaac Sim and Isaac Lab (in that order).
  --deterministic       Request reproducible rendering (see KitLauncher docs).
  --kit_args KIT_ARGS   Command line arguments for Omniverse Kit as a string
                        separated by a space delimiter. Example usage:
                        --kit_args "--ext-folder=/path/to/ext1 --ext-
                        folder=/path/to/ext2". A single Kit argument works in
                        both forms: --kit_args "--ext-folder=/path/to/ext1" or
                        --kit_args=--ext-folder=/path/to/ext1.
  --anim_recording_enabled
                        Enable recording time-sampled USD animations from
                        IsaacLab PhysX simulations.
  --anim_recording_start_time ANIM_RECORDING_START_TIME
                        Set time that animation recording begins playing. If
                        not set, the recording will start from the beginning.
  --anim_recording_stop_time ANIM_RECORDING_STOP_TIME
                        Set time that animation recording stops playing. If
                        the process is shutdown before the stop time is
                        exceeded, then the animation is not recorded.
  --max_visible_envs MAX_VISIBLE_ENVS
                        When set, caps the nums of envs shown in the launched
                        visualizers.

preset selection:
  Select named PresetCfg alternatives via Hydra-style overrides (key=value, no leading dashes):
      physics=NAME              (typed) selects a physics backend
      renderer=NAME             (typed) selects a renderer backend
      presets=NAME[,NAME,...]   broadcast: applied to every matching PresetCfg

  Pass `--task=X` along with `--help` to see preset variants available for
  that task.

  Hydra also accepts path-targeted overrides like env.sim.physics=NAME.
